<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Upper Zigzag Canyon from Timberline Lodge</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:129-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.331129" lon="-121.711243"><ele>1813.1</ele><name>Timberline Lodge</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:timberline-lodge (OSM way 149173768); confidence: high; pdf_page: 131; book_elev_ft: 5950; quote: From the lodge head west, under the Magic Mile chairlift</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.334500" lon="-121.713600"><ele>1872.2</ele><name>Under the Magic Mile chairlift</name><desc>source: OSM aerialway 5282193 Magic Mile, crossed on the diagonal northwest from the lodge that map 27's dotted line draws; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 131; quote: head west, under the Magic Mile chairlift, then climb steadily</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.338000" lon="-121.717200"><ele>1921.5</ele><name>Above the top of the Blossom chairlift</name><desc>source: just above the top of OSM aerialway 5280949 Stormin' Norman (the chair on the old Blossom line west of Magic Mile); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 131; quote: climb steadily, above the top of the Blossom chairlift</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.347000" lon="-121.718000"><ele>2084.1</ele><name>Little Zigzag Canyon crossing, near its upper end</name><desc>source: OSM Little Zigzag River way 394756863, its top node (45.34717, -121.71789); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 131; quote: Little Zigzag Canyon, 30 feet deep with steep sides. It is best crossed near its upper end</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.350800" lon="-121.720000"><ele>2152.4</ele><name>7,000-foot point on the edge of Zigzag Canyon</name><desc>source: east rim of the canyon's upper gash (OSM Zigzag River way 150578184), across from Mississippi Head (GNIS 45.3554, -121.7251, about 0.4 mi NW); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 131; book_elev_ft: 7000; quote: the 1.7-mile climb to the 7,000-foot point at the precipitous edge of Zigzag Canyon ... about even with the top of the Magic Mile chairlift ... Directly across the canyon is Mississippi Head</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Upper Zigzag Canyon from Timberline Lodge</name><desc>1. Timberline Lodge -&gt; Under the Magic Mile chairlift: straight (medium), 0.26 mi | 2. Under the Magic Mile chairlift -&gt; Above the top of the Blossom chairlift: straight (medium), 0.30 mi | 3. Above the top of the Blossom chairlift -&gt; Little Zigzag Canyon crossing, near its upper end: straight (medium), 0.62 mi | 4. Little Zigzag Canyon crossing, near its upper end -&gt; 7,000-foot point on the edge of Zigzag Canyon: straight (medium), 0.28 mi</desc>
